// GENERATED by the lens-library import (K-261; curated K-264, verified and
// re-cut K-265) - regenerate rather than edit. Prescriptions are transcribed
// patent data (photonstophotos.net Optical Bench, via the FlareSim
// collection); each file cites its patent. Factual optical tables, embedded
// as text and parsed on selection.
//
// Twenty, chosen for maximally DIFFERENT flare characters and VERIFIED:
// every entry bakes a live ghost train and keeps flaring with the light
// well off-centre (the K-265 three-position probe), because the first
// curated cut shipped lenses that looked distinct in a centred montage and
// rendered nothing in the owner's hands. Wide-angle and fisheye
// prescriptions are deliberately absent: the trace's angular acceptance
// collapses off-axis for retrofocus designs (recorded limit, docs/impl/
// lens-flare.md), and a lens that only works with a centred light is a bug
// report, not a look. A user .lens file (the `lens_file` parameter) covers
// everything else.

/// One bundled lens prescription: display name, native f-number parsed
/// from the collection filename (0.0 = unknown, estimate from geometry),
/// and the .lens text.
pub struct LensFile {
    pub name: &'static str,
    pub native_fstop: f32,
    pub text: &'static str,
}

